fetchItem, url: https://www.britannica.com/topic/samurai mergedData: {
  link: 'https://www.britannica.com/topic/samurai',
  name: 'samurai',
  description: 'SAMURAI is an open-source AI framework adapting SAM 2 for zero-shot visual object tracking in videos using motion-aware memory.',
  introduction: '## Introduction\n' +
    '\n' +
    'SAMURAI (Segment Anything Model 2 for Visual Object Tracking) is an advanced open-source artificial intelligence framework designed for zero-shot visual object tracking and segmentation in videos. By enhancing the base SAM 2 architecture with a motion-aware memory mechanism, SAMURAI achieves state-of-the-art performance in tracking target objects across complex video sequences without requiring specialized fine-tuning.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Key Features\n' +
    '\n' +
    '- **Zero-Shot Visual Object Tracking**: Tracks arbitrary objects in video streams dynamically without prior category training.\n' +
    '- **Motion-Aware Memory**: Integrates motion dynamics into memory selection to handle fast-moving objects, severe occlusions, and shape deformations.\n' +
    '- **High-Precision Segmentation**: Utilizes the power of SAM 2 to generate accurate frame-by-frame object masks.\n' +
    '- **Seamless Integration**: Provides clean APIs and pre-trained weights for research, video processing, and developer workflows.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Target Audience & Applications\n' +
    '\n' +
    'SAMURAI is ideal for computer vision researchers, video editors, autonomous vehicle engineers, and AI developers working on video segmentation, object tracking, and automated media processing.',
  categories: [ 'AI Tools', 'Developer Tools', 'Video Generation' ],
  tags: [ 'AI', 'Video', 'Open Source', 'Tech', 'Coding' ],
  image: undefined,
  icon: 'https://icons.duckduckgo.com/ip3/www.britannica.com.ico'
}
