fetchItem, url: https://tilemaker.org mergedData: {
  link: 'https://tilemaker.org',
  name: 'tilemaker',
  description: 'A command-line tool that creates vector tiles in Mapbox Vector Tile format directly from OpenStreetMap data without requiring a database stack.',
  introduction: '# tilemaker\n' +
    '\n' +
    'tilemaker is an open-source C++ command-line tool that processes OpenStreetMap (OSM) data and converts it directly into vector tiles in the industry-standard Mapbox Vector Tile (MVT) format.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Key Features\n' +
    '- **Database-Free Processing**: Generates vector tiles directly on your local machine or cloud CPU without needing PostgreSQL or complex database stacks.\n' +
    '- **Flexible Lua Scripting**: Customize tag selection, object simplification, spatial queries, and zoom-level filtering using Lua scripts.\n' +
    '- **Standalone & Lightweight**: Shipped as a single executable with pre-configured scripts for out-of-the-box tile generation.\n' +
    '- **Cross-Platform**: Builds and runs on Linux, macOS, and Windows.\n' +
    '- **Ecosystem Compatible**: Easily serve tiles via static web hosting, mbtileserver, or tileserver-php, and render them using MapLibre GL on the web, iOS, or Android.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Use Cases\n' +
    '- Creating self-hosted, custom-styled web and mobile maps (e.g., walking, cycling, or city maps).\n' +
    '- Packaging compact vector tile packages for offline map applications.\n' +
    '- Eliminating third-party map tiling API costs and vendor lock-in.',
  categories: [ 'Developer Tools', 'Data Tools' ],
  tags: [ 'Open Source', 'Tech', 'Coding' ],
